cff-version: 1.2.0
title: SAM 3 for Insects
message: >-
  If you use this software or the fine-tuned checkpoint, please cite it together
  with SAM 3 and flat-bug, on which it depends.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Adam
    family-names: Basha
    affiliation: Karlsruhe Institute of Technology
repository-code: "https://github.com/adambasha0/SAM3-for-Insects-segementation"
abstract: >-
  Detection and instance segmentation of terrestrial arthropods using Meta's
  Segment Anything 3 image model, fine-tuned on the flat-bug aggregate of 23
  insect datasets and served through flat-bug-style pyramid tiling so that small
  specimens in large trap images are recovered rather than lost to downsampling.
keywords:
  - instance segmentation
  - object detection
  - entomology
  - arthropods
  - biodiversity monitoring
  - segment anything
license-url: "https://github.com/adambasha0/SAM3-for-Insects-segementation/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: 0.1.0
references:
  - type: article
    title: "SAM 3: Segment Anything with Concepts"
    year: 2025
    authors:
      - given-names: Nicolas
        family-names: Carion
      - given-names: Laura
        family-names: Gustafson
    notes: Base model; see https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam3
  - type: article
    title: >-
      flat-bug: A General Method for Detection and Segmentation of Terrestrial
      Arthropods in Images
    journal: Methods in Ecology and Evolution
    year: 2025
    notes: >-
      Training data aggregate and the pyramid tiling methodology; see
      https://github.com/darsa-group/flat-bug
